        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"MigrantP\" data-post=\"2\" data-topic=\"29261\" data-full=\"true\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/migrantp/48/1921_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> MigrantP:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>We’re probably going to be playing it “in spirit” this coming Saturday on Spirit Island Saturday!</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Is “Spirit Island Saturday” something I should know about, or is it just a little thing with your gaming group?</p>\n<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"TakeWalker\" data-post=\"3\" data-topic=\"29261\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/takewalker/48/5677_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> TakeWalker:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I really hate that kind of thing. I find rules like that needlessly restrictive and completely against the spirit of cooperation in gameplay. <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/confused.png?v=12\" title=\":confused:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":confused:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"></p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Fair enough; I can see your point. I haven’t formed an opinion of the Scenario, as I have not yet played it.</p>",
